Tens of thousands of people will flock to Central Park for the seventh Global Citizen Festival this year to monitor the performances of artists such as Janet Jackson, Cardi B and Shawn Mendes and raise awareness of the mission of ending extreme poverty by 2030, the main target of the event.
Launched in 2012, the Global Citizen Festival is an extension of the Global Poverty Project (Governmental Poverty Project). The Global Poverty Project is an international pressure group that hopes to end poverty by increasing the number of people actively struggling with poverty.
Those who want to attend the concert have to perform certain tasks or "appointments" in order to earn a free ticket to the VIP ticket if they don't want to pay for the concert. These include voluntary voluntary, sending e-mail to world-lead leaders, searching for specific people, or carrying out other meaningful tasks that will help raise awareness about the goal of ending poverty.
