urging the British government to take action to improve maternal and juvenile child-treatening, the government announced that it will provide funding for The Power of Nutrition project and the project will reach 5 million women and children with nutritional interventions.
"Why do you think we're going to be able to end extreme poverty?"
Responsed: "It's going to be a long and difficult journey, sometimes we'll fall and fail.
But we're going to succeed because we're stronger together, like all civil rights movements and anti-discrimination movements.
